      "writtenOn": "2026-06-01T13:46:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think that this needs to have more logic put into Skia itself than relying on Chrome to correctly choose the SkYUVColorSpace. Any other client of Skia would run into these same issues. \n\nChris, do you think it\u0027s reasonable to add two enum values to `SkYUVPixmaps::DataType`, such as `kUnorm10_x6` and `kUnorm12_x4`? They would still use 16-bit color type and texture formats, but we\u0027d be conveying to Skia that the value range is not the full 16 unorm range and we could then pick the different matrices (or apply the rescaling elsewhere if need be). \n\nThen in chromium code, you would just refine the choice for the different 16bit formats.",
      "parentUuid": "3466f429_7bd8fda1",
      "revId": "6adbc5e5c3b7ee87dd754d66d0fddad7494deeb1",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
