      "writtenOn": "2026-06-11T10:02:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for tracking this down, this is great work!\n\nThe YUV\u003c-\u003eRGB matrices returned by `SkColorMatrix_YUV2RGB` assume that the inputs have already been normalized to [0,1]. And, as you\u0027ve noticed, the GPU will often be providing values normalized to [0, 65535/65472] \u003d [0, 0.999], because they\u0027re using the upper 10 bits of the 16-bit format.\n\nThis is unfortunately not universal. Hardware-based codecs tend to use the upper 10 bits of the 16-bit pixel, but software-based codecs tend to use the lower 10 bits of the 16-bit pixel. So I think having a parameter (like what Michael suggested) would be best.",
      "parentUuid": "7cf13cac_a2085f74",
      "revId": "6adbc5e5c3b7ee87dd754d66d0fddad7494deeb1",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
