      "writtenOn": "2026-06-11T10:02:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, I think that\u0027s the best solution.\n\nThe `SkYUVAPixmaps::DataType` is scoped to the `SkYUVAPixmaps`, cause it needs to go to some non-pixmap places (`GrYUVABackendTextures` and `skgpu::graphite::YUVABackendTextures`), which may be a bit messy, but is probably fine.\n\nIt also may be that we\u0027ll want to consider having both R10_X6 and X6_R10, since almost all software codecs output into the lower 10 bits (we do a bunch of extra swizzling [here](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:media/renderers/video_resource_updater.cc;l\u003d1059;drc\u003d55b4406172819a511f5f2be5e3191af91154fda3) for that).",
